  "slug": "solar-site-survey-intake-form",
  "title": "Solar Site Survey Intake Form",
  "subtitle": "An original solar site survey workflow that turns an initial request into a triaged, evidence-backed assignment, with explicit qualified-review, stop-work, escalation, and accountable handoff controls.",
  "description": "A workflow-complete solar site survey intake form for the proposed photovoltaic site that captures exact identity, domain observations, supporting evidence, decisions, exceptions, responsible owners, and closeout without replacing professional judgment or the organization's controlling procedures.",
  "use_case": "Use when a coordinator receives a new request and must verify identity, scope, evidence, hazards, feasibility, and the next accountable handoff before field activity is scheduled. The survey coordinator owns routing, and closure requires documented evidence, disposition of restrictions, and acceptance by the designated reviewer.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "intake_routing",
      "title": "Solar site survey intake identity and routing",
      "guidance": "Create one traceable intake record and assign a person responsible for triage.",
